# What must never enter the build context.
#
# The first two entries are the ones that matter. `node_modules/` would copy a macOS-resolved
# dependency tree into a Linux image and shadow the `npm ci` the Dockerfile runs — the classic way
# an image works locally and fails on the platform it was built for. `.git/` is the repository's
# whole history, which is both large and none of the image's business.

node_modules/
**/node_modules/
.git/
.gitignore

# Build output. Everything the image needs is compiled inside it, from source, so a stale local
# `dist/` must not be able to travel in and be served instead. § D201's investigation lost five
# runs to a stale `dist/`; this is the same defect closed one layer out.
dist/
**/dist/
dist-web/
**/dist-web/
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Tests, coverage and tooling — none of it runs in the image.
coverage/
**/coverage/
.worktrees/
.claude/
.github/

# Local configuration and secrets. Nothing here is committed, and nothing here may be baked into a
# layer: an image is not a secret store, and a layer is readable by anyone who can pull it.
.env
.env.*
*.local
.outbox.jsonl

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# Documentation. The image serves a simulator, not the repository.
docs/
*.md
!packages/*/README.md
